\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Spurious synergy curve generated by the seasonal observing window and linear interpolation in our negative control simulation (where the true coupling is strictly at 15 days). The false synergy rises monotonically at long lags, peaking at 197 days, exceeding the true 15-day peak. Vertical lines show the positions of the real H\(\beta \) peaks from NGC~5548.}}{14}{figure.7}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:seasonal_aliasing}{{7}{14}{Spurious synergy curve generated by the seasonal observing window and linear interpolation in our negative control simulation (where the true coupling is strictly at 15 days). The false synergy rises monotonically at long lags, peaking at 197 days, exceeding the true 15-day peak. Vertical lines show the positions of the real H\(\beta \) peaks from NGC~5548}{figure.7}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Comparison of the unconditioned (blue) and target-history conditioned (red) SURD synergy (left) and information leak (right) curves for the Core H\(\beta \) target. The orange shaded band and dashed line represent the pointwise 95\% circular-shift surrogate envelope and median at each lag for the conditioned scan. The global max-statistic test reported in the text uses a single global threshold ($0.4043$~bits) derived from the distribution of per-realization maxima and is not shown as a curve. Conditioning on the target's own past shifts the synergy peak to 73 days, but this peak is statistically insignificant (global max-statistic $p \approx 0.98$) and is driven by finite-sample bias in the sparse 4D joint probability cells.}}{14}{figure.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:history_conditioning}{{8}{14}{Comparison of the unconditioned (blue) and target-history conditioned (red) SURD synergy (left) and information leak (right) curves for the Core H\(\beta \) target. The orange shaded band and dashed line represent the pointwise 95\% circular-shift surrogate envelope and median at each lag for the conditioned scan. The global max-statistic test reported in the text uses a single global threshold ($0.4043$~bits) derived from the distribution of per-realization maxima and is not shown as a curve. Conditioning on the target's own past shifts the synergy peak to 73 days, but this peak is statistically insignificant (global max-statistic $p \approx 0.98$) and is driven by finite-sample bias in the sparse 4D joint probability cells}{figure.8}{}}
